        <h1>Hot and Bothered</h1>
        <h2>
           historically dehydrated 
        </h2>
      </div>
<h3>Ride Summary</h3>
Distance: 55 mi
<br>
Climbing: 2103 ft
<br>
Descending: similar
<br>
Difficulty: hard
<br>
<a href="https://www.strava.com/activities/18690244599">Link to workout in Strava</a>
<hr>
<a href="https://photos.app.goo.gl/J24SkNa6vuNRuvWj6">Link to photo gallery from this trip</a>
<hr>
<p>
<p>
<a href="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-dip.jpg"><img src="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-dip-small.jpg"></a>
<p>
Caught an early ferry out of Zadar, and then had 18 great low traffic island miles to the next ferry. Lori took advantage of our riding along the beach and took a dip, but I didn't feel like riding any saltier than my sweat was making me.
<p>
<a href="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-bridge.jpg"><img src="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-bridge-small.jpg"></a>
<p>
After ferry number 2 we ended up back on the main highway for an uncomfortable spell before we could get onto a parallel back road which we rode until we stumbled onto a bike campground which we stopped at for a beer but weren't quite ready for lunch nor did we manage to successfully communicate that we were interested in food to the barkeep, so we drank and rolled.
<p>
<a href="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-roadshot1.jpg"><img src="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-roadshot1-small.jpg"></a>
<p>
We freestyle re-routed onto a dirt bike route to avoid more highway which was about when the heat really kicked up. The ad-hoc routing was a success, though we did eventually end up back on the highway for a few miles before we rolled into lunchville. Language barrier thwarted our lunch order but what they made was good, even if unexpected so we ate, hydrated, and scooted down to another beach where Lori cooled down again before we took more back roads to town.
<p>
<a href="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-roadpigs.jpg"><img src="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-roadpigs-small.jpg"></a>
<p>
<i>no such Roadway Pigs were observed, fortunately?</i>
<p>
We'd re sunscreened repeatedly but were still both starting to crisp up in the broiler as we rolled down the (paved) boardwalk in the suburbs of our destination for the day, Sibenik.
<p>
<a href="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-boardwalk.jpg"><img src="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-boardwalk-small.jpg"></a>
<p>
Post-beach but before downtown where we are staying was 4 more miles of the worst highway. They just don't believe in shoulders here so we rode the white line with white knuckles and crossed the only bridge into town before we could get back onto less busy roads and climb up to drop down into old town.  Fortunately there was a "bike route" just after the bridge which we leapt onto, though it was more like a dirt backroad for people to dump trash on than a real road.  Still, we were glad for it, and we even ran across a couple of women riding towards the shitty bridge from town (that "road" went nowhere else), though not sure how they would make it across the highway as there was definitely no way to ride safely across against traffic with no shoulder!
<p>
<a href="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-stare.jpg"><img src="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-stare-small.jpg"></a>
<a href="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-umbrella.jpg"><img src="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-umbrella-small.jpg"></a>
<p>
We walked our bikes through more than one restaurant (they fill the alleys and squares in this town) to find our apartment which is again a historical building from centuries ago. Fortunately, the plumbing and air conditioning are modern!  Our landlord recommended a local-flavors place and we enjoyed some of that local flavor - Lori and I both had amazing <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pa%C5%A1ticada">Pasticada</a> which led to several additional similar orders at future restaurants - none of which were nearly as good as this first batch - before THE EXCITEMENT OF LAUNDRY TIME.
<p>
<a href="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-churchpark.jpg"><img src="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-churchpark-small.jpg"></a>
<a href="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-wallmap.jpg"><img src="https://q42.me/trips/europe2026/sibenik-wallmap-small.jpg"></a>
<p>
